<section class="code-project">
  <h2>Python Active-subspaces Utility Library</h2>
  <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary)">A Python library for discovering and exploiting active subspaces in computational models. Provides tools for gradient-based dimension reduction, sufficient summary plots, and response surface construction.</p>
  <div class="project-links">
    <a href="https://github.com/zgrey/active_subspaces">GitHub</a>
    <a href="https://joss.theoj.org/papers/10.21105/joss.00079">JOSS Paper</a>
  </div>
  <div class="project-refs">
    <h3>Key references</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Grey &amp; Constantine (2018). <a href="https://arc.aiaa.org/doi/10.2514/1.J056054">Active subspaces of airfoil shape parameterizations</a>. <em>AIAA Journal</em> 56(5), 2003&ndash;2017. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.02909">arXiv:1702.02909</a></li>
    </ul>
